In article <383B6AA9.611265B5@swecexc.xko.dec.com>, GopalKrishna Prasad
<prasad@swecexc.xko.dec.com> wrote:

>    I want to extract amount of free space available on a disk (for
>example rz0). How can I do this in a C program ?

use the statvfs() or statfs() system calls.  

statvfs() is the POSIX standard way to do this, however, it lacks some
host OS specific features.  The statvfs structure is defined in the
<sys/statvfs.h> header file.

statfs() is what is used by the df utility, but the values that it
returns may not be available on all UNIX implementations.  The statfs
structure is defined in the <sys/mount.h> header file.



