>   I have lots of documents in DecWrite, which I now need to have in a
> format that someone else can actually read (i.e., MicroSoft Word or
> WordPerfect).

If you have the CDA converters on your machine, you should be able to :

$CONVERT/DOCUMENT mydecwrite.ddif/format=ddif myword.doc/format=word5

some of the formats supported for output:
macwrite
rtf
sgml
wordp
word5
text
wpl	(wpsplus)

(This assumes you are running VMS)

Obviously, you'd probably lose plenty of formatting information but your
documents should be usable/readable on the target machine.



