Actually, ppp isn't a server-client-connection. As soon as the connection is
establisht to another machine, your machine should be a reachable
equivalently treated computer in the internet, so to say hooked in via the
'server'. Note that all tcp/ip actions via the ppp-line may happen in both
directions (ftp, telnet, rlogin, ...)

I suppose, you haven't configured your underlaying scripts well:
/etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hosts on the 'client'...

Testing: Try ping yyy.yyy.yyy.yy  to a machine using the numerical ip despite
your 'server'-machine to check wether the connection is ok
When all packages are transfered well, you have to tell your 'client' how to
find the other machines by lexical name . E.g., if you are connected to a
nameserver:

/etc/resolv.conf:
nameserver xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx

(the xxx_s  stand for the nameserver's ip)

Best regards
Olli



