Look for a file called /etc/.AM_is_running

If it exists, delete it. It seems to act as a flag to prevent more then
one person editing your passwd file at the same time.

Often what happens is someone with admin privilages has dxaccounts open
-which creates that dummy file. The machine either gets re-set, or the
person's connection dies and that file ends up sticking around. The
system ends up thinking the files are locked

Try it

James


