Burkhard Schultheis <bschultheis@tde-online.de> writes:

>we use some NFS mounting on DEC UNIX 4.0b (export and import is on this
>version). We see very poor write performance. Is there a trick to boost
>write performance (we will upgrade to UNIX 4.0e in the next weeks)?

What performance are you seeing?  It should be no higher than your
disk performance.  You should be using NFS V3, but verify that
(mount | grep v3).  If you are using Gigabit Ethernet (we may
not support that on V4.0B), you may need a patch.

Why are you upgrading to V4.0E?  V4.0F has a number of little performance
improvements that help NFS (faster IP checksum, faster disk name cache,
NFS V3's READDIRPLUS code is lean).

