darkone wrote:
> 
> Dear All,
> 
> I am trying to set-up a remote printer on a DU4.0d machine. The printer
> is a normal HPLJ4 or HPLJ5Si running on a novell network and the
> connection would be via TCP/IP. Has anyone done this or know's how to. I
> have the printer printing but all I get is a header for the job on one
> page and one line of the file on the next.....???

You can avoid the header stuff by using the sp (supress header) option
in your printcap file.
Regarding the one line, I suppose it's the well known CR/LF thing.

Possible solutions are :

Most HP printers have an option where they by themselves add a carriage
return when they se a line feed.

HP print servers have a extra spool queue called text. This'll do the
same, but you need to have the printers sitting on a HP printserver.

Third solution is to have a 2nd queue on your unix box. Problem is you
can't make print filters on a remote queue, so you make a local queue
with filters and redirect its output to the remote queue.



l8r/Jspr



