I don't know if it is because the video card is unsupported,
but if you want to do a text based installation, then take out the
video card, keyboard and mouse, then plug in a serial console and
do the configuration. Before you do this though you need to tell
the firmware that you intend to switch to a serial console by
typing 'set console serial' at the >>> prompt and then type 'init'
or press the reset switch.
To return to your current configuration use 'set console graphics'.
(You may have to do this blind).
Hope this helps
Adam.
PS. One other thought is that your monitor may not support the
graphics mode that the install is trying to run?
