No, /etc/services is just a name for the port, nothing more. But what
can happen is that if the server is shut down withou cleanly closing the
socket, the socket can go into TIME_WAIT which will prevent a new bind
without specifying the SO_REUSEADDR. Six hours should be long enough
though...
Try doing a netstat -an >/tmp/sockets.list just before starting the
servers, check if the failed servers correspond to open sockets...

/WB/

