Mark Orndorff wrote:
> 
> I am trying to connect to the serial port on a DS10 with a direct connection
> to COM1  on my NT. Usinf hyperterminal for emulation. I can't get the
> connection to work for RMC or the console settings as follows:
> 
> BPS            9600
> Data bits    8
> Parity          None
> Stop Bits    1
> Floe control    I've tried Hardware
>                                           Xon/Xoff
>                                           none
> I can't seem to make this work. Any ideas?

First, are you using a standard-everyday serial cable? You'll need a
"null-modem adapter" connected inline.

Next, have you set up the COM port on the D/T64 UNIX box as a terminal
device? Assuming you want to hook up to COM1, edit /etc/inittab to
include the line:

	terminal:023:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty /dev/tty00 9600 vt100

If you want to be able to login to root, edit /etc/securettys to
include:

	/dev/tty00

Once you made the changes, do an "init q" from root. 

Then set HyperTerm for 9600 BPS, 8-bit, no parity, 1 stop bit... Might
have to mess with the flow control (hardware perhaps??).
-- 

