Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.misc,comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.admin,comp.mail.uucp

Found problem, thanks to all whom sent comments.

UUCP being an older protocol has a 7 chariter host name limit.  It does
handle longer names, but not well.  Ours are set up in "groups" with the
name of the group being 7 to 8 letters and a 8th or 9th number
indicating which one of the group.  So two systems of the same group
cannot not talk to each other, but this is not a problem.




