I don't remember what halt code 5 means, but :
If you do a show power from the boot prompt, does it contain logs entrys
with power suppply fan failures around the same time your machine
crashed ?

If it does, do you have firmware < 5.5 ?


Reason why I ask is because we've had similar problems with some AS1200
machines. They halted without any reason and without logging anything in
unix.
When we investigated the power log, it said the PSU or CPU fan had
failed. This was false.
I turned out to be the firmware and/or the fans who reported failure
even though they didn't fail. This caused the machine to shut down to
prevent damage to the rest of the hardware.
With firmware 5.5 this problem is fixed by (as far as I'm informed)
making the firmware more tolerant, so it doesn't halt the machine just
because one fan reports failure for a short period.


l8r/Jspr



