In article <38219013.2D29C469@linmpi.mpg.de>,
Helmut Michels  <michels@linmpi.mpg.de> wrote:
> How can I remove a retired user from the system with the enhanced
> security subsets installed. I want to re-use  username and UID.

1) Submit an enhancement request with Compaq, asking for a way
to make `userdel' actually delete a user even if C2 security
is enabled.  They're following the C2 spec very closely here,
and the problem is that it states that objects are never to be
re-used (they can only be retired).

IMHO, For standards conformance retiring users should definitely
be the default, but there should also definitely be a way to
override the default and actually delete the user.

2) Use `userdel' from from a 4.0b patchlevel 3 or earlier system.
It allowed complete deletion of a user, even on C2 systems.

3) If you're only talking about a couple people, you can do it
the hard way:

	mkdir /etc/ptmp
	vi /etc/passwd
	<*carefully* delete the lines, and save the file>
	rmdir /etc/ptmp
	mkpasswd /etc/passwd

You can't use `vipw' because it will complain that you mangled
the temp file.

Tim
